    description: "The T 6.5 S runs a 2.6 CHP motor against a 20 by 55-inch belt, with motorised incline to 10%, a top speed of 10 mph and a published 300 lb capacity. The console is a five-inch backlit display with roughly twenty onboard programmes, iFit-enabled and typically shipped with a trial membership, and it folds vertically with a lift-assisted mechanism. The hardware is ordinary for the price and coherent for walking. The thing to understand before buying is that NordicTrack is a content company selling equipment, the screen is the product being marketed, and at five inches this particular screen is a poor vehicle for the content it is advertising — which is why it is worth buying for what it does manually rather than for what the platform promises. It takes the slot the C950i itself held on this page: the C950i is discontinued and sold only used, mostly on local marketplaces rather than Amazon, and the T 6.5 S is the cheapest new NordicTrack we found on Amazon. Its 55-inch deck is shorter than the C950i's 60 inches, so for running look at the T Series 10 below.",
  },
  {
    id: "nordictrack-t-series-10",
    name: "NordicTrack T Series 10",
    brand: "NordicTrack",
    category: "Closest Current Folding Equivalent",
    badge: "Closest Replacement",
