            <a href="#nordictrack-t-6-5-s" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">NordicTrack T 6.5 S</a>
            <a href="#nordictrack-t-6-5-s" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">Closest Replacement:</span>
            <a href="#nordictrack-t-series-10" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">NordicTrack T Series 10</a>
            <a href="#nordictrack-t-series-10" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">Step Up:</span>
            <a href="#nordictrack-commercial-1250" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">NordicTrack Commercial 1250</a>
            <a href="#nordictrack-commercial-1250" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-4">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-[#FF5A1F]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h7"></path></svg>
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#short-answer" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">1. NordicTrack C950i: The Short Answer</a>
          <a href="#what-it-was" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">2. What the C950i Was</a>
          <a href="#specifications" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">3. C950i Specifications: What Is Known</a>
          <a href="#ifit" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">4. iFIT on a C950i in 2026</a>
          <a href="#parts" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">5. Parts and Repairs</a>
          <a href="#buying-used" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">6. Buying a Used NordicTrack C950i</a>
          <a href="#replacements" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">7. What Replaced the C950i</a>
          <a href="#verdict" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">8. Should You Buy a NordicTrack C950i?</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">9. Frequently Asked Questions</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          The NordicTrack C950i is a folding treadmill that NordicTrack no longer makes or sells. It still
          turns up on local marketplaces, and people who search for it are usually deciding whether a used
          one is worth the asking price, or whether the one in their basement is worth repairing. The
          honest answer depends on three things this page covers: what the machine was when new, which is
          documented thinly; what iFIT’s decision to end support for older machines in 2023 means for its
          console; and whether the parts that wear out can still be found. We end with the current
          NordicTrack models that do the same job new.
        </p>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">1. NordicTrack C950i: The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>The NordicTrack C950i is discontinued, so the only way to buy one is used, and a used one
            is only worth buying cheaply, after a proper test, and on the understanding that it is a manual
            treadmill now.</strong> iFIT ended support for older-generation machines on 30 April 2023; machines
            that lost support still run in manual mode with their preloaded workouts.
          </p>
          <p>
            What made the C950i appealing when new still holds: a full 20 by 60-inch belt on a folding frame,
            with built-in programs. What counts against it is age, a thinly documented specification, and the
            one full independent review we found, which judged it a decent walking treadmill with a powerful
            motor but a frame that felt wobbly at incline for heavier runners.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you want the same kind of machine new, NordicTrack’s T Series 10 is the closest current
            equivalent and the Commercial 1250 the sturdier step up. Because a C950i can only be bought used,
            and mostly not on Amazon, the cards below start with the cheapest new NordicTrack on Amazon, the
            T 6.5 S, as the price point to weigh a used C950i against. We have not tested any of them.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Product cards -->
      <div class="not-prose">
